# Project rules

Read `AGENTS.md` first — it is the single source of truth for stack, commands, conventions, and the Definition of Done.

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Dev server | `pnpm dev` |
| Build | `pnpm build` |
| Typecheck | `pnpm typecheck` |
| Lint | `pnpm lint` |
| Tests | `pnpm test` |
| All gates | `pnpm validate` |

## Hard rules

- Stack: Astro 7, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`), pnpm. Do not introduce other frameworks or package managers.
- Package manager is pnpm — never generate `package-lock.json` or `yarn.lock`.
- Never edit `dist/`, `.astro/`, `node_modules/`, or `pnpm-lock.yaml` directly.
- Never edit `session-*.md` or `plan.txt`.
- Do not modify `biome.json` unless explicitly asked (config is settled).
- Commits follow Conventional Commits (enforced by lefthook commit-msg hook).

## Definition of Done

Before declaring any task complete, `pnpm validate` must pass, new logic needs tests in `src/**/*.test.ts`, and behavior changes require doc updates (`AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/*`).

## Known pitfalls

- Biome `--write` on `.astro` frontmatter is not idempotent (biomejs/biome#7912). Lint `.astro` read-only; never apply `lint:fix:unsafe` to them.
- Site is served under base path `/blaise-web` (GitHub Pages project site). All internal links must be base-path-aware (`withBase()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` or `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`).
